AB  - Large Language Model (LLM) plays a crucial role in the taxation domain, in spite of their occasional tendency to provide unreliable answers. As the Indonesian income tax system is highly complicated, this study introduces BeeTax, an Indonesian Withholding Tax Article 21 (WHT Article 21) chatbot that leverages Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to support users in understanding theoretical taxation concepts, and function calling to automate tax calculations. While prior studies have shown that RAG and function calling each improve the accuracy and reliability of LLMs, they have mainly been examined separately. BeeTax bridges this gap by integrating both mechanisms within a unified architecture, demonstrating their mutual benefit in a domain-specific application. The chatbot achieved Retrieval Augmented Generation Assessment (RAGAs) scores of 0.71 (faithfulness), 0.81 (answer relevancy), 0.61 (answer correctness), and 0.79 (context precision and recall), indicating reliable retrieval and high generation accuracy in a technical tax domain. The function-calling mechanism achieved 91 % accuracy, confirming its high consistency in performing tax computations. The qualitative evaluations through experts' User Acceptance Testing (UAT) yielded pass rates of 85.71 % and 95.24 %, while a user survey assessing four usability aspects reported satisfaction scores of at least 4.57 out of 5. Overall, the results confirm that combining RAG and function calling improves the user experience, making BeeTax a practical and accessible Artificial Intelligence (AI) solution for WHT Article 21 assistance.
