AB  - This research presents a novel solution for the challenges associated with the conventional static training processes adopted by domain-specific chatbots (DSCs) through the development of a self-improvement system using the low-rank adaptation approach on the Flan-T5 large language model. Typically, the training processes adopted by DSCs involve the usage of updated data sets, which is not feasible on a regular basis. However, the self-enhancement approach presented in this research utilizes the capabilities of the continuous learning processes with the support of real-time users. This solution is developed through the identification of the need for the improvement of user queries and the usage of the low-rank adaptation approach for the highly efficient updating of the model with only 0.1% parameters updated. The results presented through the evaluation of the solution indicate a significant improvement in the correctness of the chatbot responses by up to 28% during the dynamic query testing and a user satisfaction rate of 92%, marking a significant improvement in the field of chatbots and establishing a new standard for the operation of a highly adaptable, context-sensitive, and proficient domain-specific chatbots.
