AB  - Rising global energy demand and the inaccessibility of conventional management tools highlight the urgent need for intelligent, user-friendly advisory systems. Standalone Large Language Models (LLMs) are prone to domain-specific hallucinations, limiting their reliability in energy applications. This work proposes a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) powered chatbot that couples a React-Flask conversational interface with a FAISS vector database, grounding responses in verified sources including the UK-DALE and UCI Smart Meter datasets. User queries are encoded into 384-dimensional dense vectors via all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and matched against curated energy knowledge before generation. Evaluation across 100 domain-specific queries yields a factual faithfulness score of 94.2% and a hallucination rate of 3.5%, outperforming standalone LLMs by 25.8 and 18.6 percentage points respectively. These results confirm that retrieval-grounded generation is essential for trustworthy conversational energy management.
